## Problem Statement

Given `n` buildings and a set of height restrictions, determine the maximum possible height of the tallest building while satisfying all constraints.

---

## My Approach

### Idea

- Add Building 1 with height 0 as a mandatory restriction.
- Sort all restrictions by building index.
- Traverse left to right to limit heights based on previous buildings.
- Traverse right to left to enforce constraints from the opposite direction.
- For every adjacent pair of restrictions, compute the highest possible peak between them.

---

## Complexity Analysis

```text
Time Complexity : O(m log m)

Space Complexity: O(m)
```

where `m` is the number of restrictions.

